0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-three-store-traits","title":"The three store traits, and which one you implement"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-scheduler-traits-are-split-by-caller","title":"The scheduler traits are split by caller"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-error-model","title":"The error model"},{"depth":2,"url":"#async-tokio-spawn-is-banned","title":["Async: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"tokio::spawn"}]," is banned"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#two-metric-systems","title":"Two metric systems"},{"depth":2,"url":"#lints-formatting-and-the-small-stuff","title":"Lints, formatting and the small stuff"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Codebase internals"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"The traits, the error model, the async rules and the two metric systems: the conventions a reviewer will assume you already know."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone about to write Forge code rather than read\nit. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," the four things that are enforced\nrather than suggested: the store trait split, the error model, the\nspawning rules, and which metric system to use. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," thirty minutes."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Most of Forge's review feedback is about conventions, not logic. The\nconventions are strong, mostly mechanically enforced, and each one exists\nfor a reason you can point at in the source. This page is the set of them\nthat a first contribution reliably trips over."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The repository targets Rust edition 2024 with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"rust-version = \"1.97.1\""}],"."]}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-three-store-traits","children":"The three store traits, and which one you implement"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Three of them exist, and they are not interchangeable."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreDriver"}]}],"\n(",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-util/src/store_trait.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-util/src/store_trait.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-util/src/store_trait.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"StoreDriver"]}],")\nis the one you implement. Its supertraits are\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"Sync + Send + Unpin + MetricsComponent + HealthStatusIndicator + 'static"}],",\nso a new store is observable and health-checkable by construction, not by\nremembering to add it."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"Store"}]}]," is a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"#[repr(transparent)]"}]," newtype over ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Arc<dyn StoreDriver>"}],".\nIt is what everything else holds."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreLike"}]}]," is the caller-facing surface: two required methods, every\nconvenience built on top of them as a default, and blanket impls so that\nboth ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Store"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"impl StoreDriver"}]," satisfy it. You call ",["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreLike"}],"; you\nimplement ",["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreDriver"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"StoreDriver"}]," methods you must supply are ","$L7",",\n","$L8",", ","$L9",", ","$La",", ","$Lb",", ","$Lc",",\n","$Ld"," and ","$Le","."]}],"\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a","\n","$L3b"]}],"$L3c"]}],["$L3d","$L3e"],"$L3f"]}],"isPartial":"$@40","staleTime":"$41","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L42","isPartial":"$@43","staleTime":"$41","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L44","isPartial":"$@45","staleTime":"$41","varyParams":"$46"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@47","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@48"}
